\"none\">t</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">y</text><polyline points=\"46,39 49,39 52,39 55.1,39 58.1,39 61.1,39 64.1,39 67.2,39 70.2,39 73.2,39 76.2,39 79.2,39 82.3,39 85.3,39 88.3,39 91.3,39 94.4,39 97.4,39 100.4,39 103.4,39 106.4,39 109.5,39 112.5,39 115.5,39 118.5,39 121.6,39 124.6,39 127.6,39 130.6,39 133.6,39 136.7,39 139.7,39 142.7,39 145.7,39 148.8,39 151.8,39 154.8,132.9 157.8,132.9 160.8,132.9 163.9,132.9 166.9,132.9 169.9,132.9 172.9,132.9 176,132.9 179,132.9 182,132.9 185,132.9 188,132.9 191.1,132.9 194.1,132.9 197.1,132.9 200.1,132.9 203.2,132.9 206.2,132.9 209.2,132.9 212.2,132.9 215.2,132.9 218.3,132.9 221.3,132.9 224.3,132.9 227.3,132.9 230.4,132.9 233.4,132.9 236.4,132.9 239.4,132.9 242.4,132.9 245.5,132.9 248.5,132.9 251.5,132.9 254.5,132.9 257.6,132.9 260.6,132.9 263.6,132.9 266.6,132.9 269.6,132.9 272.7,132.9 275.7,132.9 278.7,132.9 281.7,132.9 284.8,132.9 287.8,132.9 290.8,132.9 293.8,132.9 296.8,132.9 299.9,132.9 302.9,132.9 305.9,132.9 308.9,132.9 312,132.9 315,132.9 318,132.9\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"/></svg>","figure_alt":"A rectangular pulse with no height or width written on it."},{"id":"step-resp-r2-q5","version":1,"round":2,"type":"numeric","prompt":"A unit-DC-gain system with \\(\\tau=2\\ \\mathrm{s}\\) starts at rest. The input is a pulse of height 4 from \\(t=0\\) to \\(t=1\\ \\mathrm{s}\\), then 0. The pulse is a step minus a delayed step. What is the output at \\(t=1.5\\ \\mathrm{s}\\)?","answer":1.22574,"unit":"(unitless)","tolerance":0.02,"explanation":"Up to 1 s the input is a step of height 4, so \\(y(1)=4(1-e^{-0.5})\\). From 1 s to 1.5 s the input is 0, which is the same as subtracting a step of height 4 that started at 1 s. The value already reached then decays for 0.5 s: multiply by \\(e^{-0.25}\\). Continuing to charge toward 4 forgets that the pulse has ended.","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 176\" role=\"img\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\"><title>pulse</title><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"146\"/><polygon points=\"318,146 311.6,148.7 311.6,143.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"46\" y2=\"24\"/><polygon points=\"46,24 48.7,30.4 43.3,30.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"318\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">t</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">y</text><polyline points=\"46,132.9 49,126.3 52,120.1 55.1,114.1 58.1,108.4 61.1,102.9 64.1,97.7 67.2,92.6 70.2,87.9 73.2,83.3 76.2,78.9 79.2,74.7 82.3,70.7 85.3,66.8 88.3,63.2 91.3,59.7 94.4,56.3 97.4,53.1 100.4,50 103.4,47.1 106.4,44.3 109.5,41.6 112.5,39 115.5,39.9 118.5,43.9 121.6,47.8 124.6,51.5 127.6,55 130.6,58.4 133.6,61.6 136.7,64.7 139.7,67.7 142.7,70.5 145.7,73.2 148.8,75.8 151.8,78.3 154.8,80.7 157.8,82.9 160.8,85.1 163.9,87.2 166.9,89.2 169.9,91.1 172.9,92.9 176,94.6 179,96.3 182,97.9 185,99.4 188,100.9 191.1,102.2 194.1,103.6 197.1,104.9 200.1,106.1 203.2,107.2 206.2,108.3 209.2,109.4 212.2,110.4 215.2,111.4 218.3,112.3 221.3,113.2 224.3,114.1 227.3,114.9 230.4,115.7 233.4,116.4 236.4,117.1 239.4,117.8 242.4,118.5 245.5,119.1 248.5,119.7 251.5,120.3 254.5,120.8 257.6,121.3 260.6,121.8 263.6,122.3 266.6,122.8 269.6,123.2 272.7,123.6 275.7,124 278.7,124.4 281.7,124.8 284.8,125.1 287.8,125.5 290.8,125.8 293.8,126.1 296.8,126.4 299.9,126.7 302.9,126.9 305.9,127.2 308.9,127.5 312,127.7 315,127.9 318,128.1\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"/></svg>","figure_alt":"A curve that rises and then falls back toward the axis."},{"id":"step-resp-r2-q6","version":1,"round":2,"type":"error","prompt":"A pulse of height \\(A\\) runs from time 0 to time \\(T\\). A student builds it from steps. Exactly one step is wrong.","explanation":"The difference of steps is the right input. Before time \\(T\\) the delayed step is still zero, so subtracting it early removes a response that has not started. After \\(T\\) the subtraction is required.","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 176\" role=\"img\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\"><title>pulse</title><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"146\"/><polygon points=\"318,146 311.6,148.7 311.6,143.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"46\" y2=\"24\"/><polygon points=\"46,24 48.7,30.4 43.3,30.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"318\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">t</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">y</text><polyline points=\"46,132.9 49,126.3 52,120.1 55.1,114.1 58.1,108.4 61.1,102.9 64.1,97.7 67.2,92.6 70.2,87.9 73.2,83.3 76.2,78.9 79.2,74.7 82.3,70.7 85.3,66.8 88.3,63.2 91.3,59.7 94.4,56.3 97.4,53.1 100.4,50 103.4,47.1 106.4,44.3 109.5,41.6 112.5,39 115.5,39.9 118.5,43.9 121.6,47.8 124.6,51.5 127.6,55 130.6,58.4 133.6,61.6 136.7,64.7 139.7,67.7 142.7,70.5 145.7,73.2 148.8,75.8 151.8,78.3 154.8,80.7 157.8,82.9 160.8,85.1 163.9,87.2 166.9,89.2 169.9,91.1 172.9,92.9 176,94.6 179,96.3 182,97.9 185,99.4 188,100.9 191.1,102.2 194.1,103.6 197.1,104.9 200.1,106.1 203.2,107.2 206.2,108.3 209.2,109.4 212.2,110.4 215.2,111.4 218.3,112.3 221.3,113.2 224.3,114.1 227.3,114.9 230.4,115.7 233.4,116.4 236.4,117.1 239.4,117.8 242.4,118.5 245.5,119.1 248.5,119.7 251.5,120.3 254.5,120.8 257.6,121.3 260.6,121.8 263.6,122.3 266.6,122.8 269.6,123.2 272.7,123.6 275.7,124 278.7,124.4 281.7,124.8 284.8,125.1 287.8,125.5 290.8,125.8 293.8,126.1 296.8,126.4 299.9,126.7 302.9,126.9 305.9,127.2 308.9,127.5 312,127.7 315,127.9 318,128.1\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"/></svg>","figure_alt":"A curve that rises and later falls, with no time labels.","steps":["The pulse equals a step of height \\(A\\) at time 0 minus a step of height \\(A\\) at time \\(T\\).","Call the unit-step response \\(s(t)\\). Linearity scales it by \\(A\\).","For \\(0<t<T\\) only the first step has arrived, so the output is \\(A\\,s(t)\\).","During \\(0<t<T\\) subtract \\(A\\,s(t-T)\\) as well."],"flaw_index":3,"reasons":["The delayed step is zero until time \\(T\\), so it must not be subtracted on \\(0<t<T\\).","The two steps should be added, not subtracted.","A pulse is a single step of height \\(A\\times T\\)."],"correct_reason":0},{"id":"step-resp-r3-q4","version":1,"round":3,"type":"mc","prompt":"A pulse of height 5 is on from \\(t=1\\) to \\(t=4\\) and is zero otherwise. Which difference of steps is that input? \\(u\\) is the unit step.","options":["\\(5u(t-1)-5u(t-4)\\)","\\(5u(t)-5u(t-4)\\)","\\(5u(t-1)+5u(t-4)\\)","\\(u(t-1)-u(t-4)\\)"],"correct_index":0,"explanation":"The pulse turns on at \\(t=1\\) and turns off at \\(t=4\\), so the second step is delayed by 4 and subtracted. A step at time 0 starts too early. Adding the second step doubles the height after \\(t=4\\) instead of returning to zero. Dropping the 5 is a pulse of height 1.","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 176\" role=\"img\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\"><title>held pulse</title><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"146\"/><polygon points=\"318,146 311.6,148.7 311.6,143.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"46\" y2=\"24\"/><polygon points=\"46,24 48.7,30.4 43.3,30.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"318\" y=\"162\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">t</text><text x=\"50\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">y</text><polyline points=\"46,39 49,39 52,39 55.1,39 58.1,39 61.1,39 64.1,39 67.2,39 70.2,39 73.2,39 76.2,39 79.2,39 82.3,39 85.3,39 88.3,39 91.3,39 94.4,39 97.4,39 100.4,39 103.4,39 106.4,39 109.5,39 112.5,39 115.5,39 118.5,39 121.6,39 124.6,39 127.6,39 130.6,39 133.6,39 136.7,39 139.7,39 142.7,39 145.7,39 148.8,39 151.8,39 154.8,132.9 157.8,132.9 160.8,132.9 163.9,132.9 166.9,132.9 169.9,132.9 172.9,132.9 176,132.9 179,132.9 182,132.9 185,132.9 188,132.9 191.1,132.9 194.1,132.9 197.1,132.9 200.1,132.9 203.2,132.9 206.2,132.9 209.2,132.9 212.2,132.9 215.2,132.9 218.3,132.9 221.3,132.9 224.3,132.9 227.3,132.9 230.4,132.9 233.4,132.9 236.4,132.9 239.4,132.9 242.4,132.9 245.5,132.9 248.5,132.9 251.5,132.9 254.5,132.9 257.6,132.9 260.6,132.9 263.6,132.9 266.6,132.9 269.6,132.9 272.7,132.9 275.7,132.9 278.7,132.9 281.7,132.9 284.8,132.9 287.8,132.9 290.8,132.9 293.8,132.9 296.8,132.9 299.9,132.9 302.9,132.9 305.9,132.9 308.9,132.9 312,132.9 315,132.9 318,132.9\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"/></svg>","figure_alt":"A rectangular pulse sitting away from the time origin."},{"id":"step-resp-r3-q5","version":1,"round":3,"type":"numeric","prompt":"A unit-DC-gain system with \\(\\tau=1\\ \\mathrm{s}\\) starts at rest. The input is a pulse of height 2 from \\(t=0\\) to \\(t=0.5\\ \\mathrm{s}\\). What is the output at \\(t=1.5\\ \\mathrm{s}\\)?","answer":0.289499,"unit":"(unitless)","tolerance":0.02,"explanation":"At the end of the pulse, \\(y(0.5)=2(1-e^{-0.5})\\). The input is then zero for one more second, so that value decays by \\(e^{-1}\\). The expression \\(2(1-e^{-1.5})\\) would be a step that never turned off.","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 176\" role=\"img\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\"><title>pulse</title><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"318\" y2=\"146\"/><polygon points=\"318,146 311.6,148.7 311.6,143.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"46\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"46\" y2=\"24\"/><polygon points=